@page "/components/typography"

<PageTitle>Typography — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Typography</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    shadcn's page here is a set of classes to copy, not a component, and this port ships none: prose is the application's, and a design system that styles every <code>&lt;p&gt;</code> fights the page it is embedded in. What the library does own is the two type tokens — <code>--control-text</code> for controls and <code>--font-numeric</code> for figures that have to line up in a column. A theme may also set <code>--font-sans</code>, <code>--font-mono</code> and <code>--tracking-normal</code>; see <a href="/theming">Theming</a>.
</p>


